            "id": "4964269",
            "title": "Anthropic IPO Roadshow Takes Center Stage As Earnings Take A Breather",
            "description": "<html><body><p class=\"MsoNormal\" data-eci=\"true\">Get ahead of the market by subscribing to Seeking Alpha's Wall Street Week Ahead, a preview of key events scheduled for the coming week. The newsletter keeps you informed of the biggest stories set to make headlines, including upcoming IPOs, investor days, earnings reports, and conference presentations.</p> <p class=\"MsoNormal\">Wall Street's major averages were mixed on Friday, as the S&amp;P 500 (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/SP500\" title=\"S&amp;P 500 Index\">SP500</a>) and the Nasdaq (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/COMP:IND\" title=\"NASDAQ Composite Index\">COMP:IND</a>) tried to recover from a persistent technology-led selloff. AI-related stocks such as Advanced Micro Devices (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/AMD\" title=\"Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.\">AMD</a>), Sandisk (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/SNDK\" title=\"Sandisk Corporation\">SNDK</a>), Micron Technology (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/MU\" title=\"Micron Technology, Inc.\">MU</a>), and Dell Technologies (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/DELL\" title=\"Dell Technologies Inc.\">DELL</a>) rose after days of declines. On the economic front, nonfarm payrolls surged in October, sending the unemployment rate lower.</p> <p class=\"MsoNormal\">The next week will kick off with speeches from several members of the Federal Reserve, including Michelle Bowman, Austan Goolsbee, and Thomas Barkin on Monday, who are expected to speak on the overall economic condition and provide clues on future monetary policy. Other Fed members, including Governor Christopher Waller and Mary Daly, are also scheduled to speak later in the week. Inflation data for the month of October is due on Tuesday, with jobless claims numbers and existing home sales for October scheduled for Thursday. October PPI data and the monthly IEA report will be released on Friday.</p> <p class=\"MsoNormal\">